title: 'For Cleo: skg-for-ai''s ''view'' now handles ''(switch-to-view ID)''; the forest commands still refuse it, with a clear error.'
pid: 2580a4e2-89f3-4d99-bad1-b3461ff1552c
body: |2-
  'containers ID', 'links-here ID' and 'forest KIND ID' raise the same
  explanation instead of printing another view's files, since they draw
  a folder the landed view may not hold. Also: 'view U', when the
  daemon already holds a view of U and another view whose perspective
  put U at its root, first closes the view of U (as before this change)
  and then lands in the other; the old files of U are marked closed.
  Rare, and older than this change.
